  "summary": "The Ahar rug, also known as Ahar carpet, is a type of Persian carpet made in the town of Ahar, located in the town of Ahar County which was  the capital of Karadag Khanate in Iran.",
  "description": "The Ahar rug, also known as Ahar carpet, is a type of Persian carpet made in the town of Ahar, located in the town of Ahar County which was  the capital of Karadag Khanate in Iran.\n\nThe name of the rug references the city and region of origin.",
  "culturalContext": "Over the last 30 years, Ahar rugs have emerged as a recognizable group in the marketplace, and they are sold in many parts of Iran outside their town of origin.",
